        <title>Vault Backup — Privacy Policy</title>                                                
      </head>                                                                                       
      <body>                                                                                        
        <main>                                                                                      
          <h1>Vault Backup Privacy Policy</h1>                                                      
          <h2>Purpose and operator</h2>                                                             
          <p>                                                                                       
            Vault Backup is a private, single-user backup utility operated                          
            by the owner of the thalsdj GitHub account. It is not offered                           
            as a public service.                                                                    
          </p>                                                                                      
          <h2>Google account access</h2>                                                            
          <p>                                                                                       
            The operator authorises Rclone to access Google Drive for                               
            storing and managing a personal Restic backup repository.                               
            Access is used to create, list, read, and delete backup                                 
            repository files as needed for backup, maintenance, and recovery.                       
            This utility does not request Gmail or Google Calendar access.                          
          </p>                                                                                      
          <h2>Data storage and protection</h2>                                                      
          <p>                                                                                       
            Restic encrypts backup contents and file metadata before upload.                        
            Encrypted repository data is stored in the operator's Google                            
            Drive. Google processes account and storage information under                           
            its own terms and privacy policy.                                                       
          </p>                                                                                      
          <p>                                                                                       
            OAuth credentials and the backup password are kept in private                           
            storage controlled by the operator. They are not published on                           
            this website or in its public GitHub repository.                                        
          </p>                                                                                      
          <h2>Sharing and use</h2>                                                                  
          <p>                                                                                       
            The operator does not sell Google user data, use it for                                 
            advertising, or intentionally share it with other users.                                
            Google user data is not used to train artificial intelligence                           
            or machine-learning models.                                                             
          </p>                                                                                      
          <p>                                                                                       
            Vault Backup's use and transfer of information received from                            
            Google APIs adheres to the Google API Services User Data Policy,                        
            including its Limited Use requirements.                                                 
          </p>                                                                                      
          <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>                                                           
          <p>                                                                                       
            Backups remain until the operator removes them using backup                             
            retention tools or deletes the repository. Google Drive trash                           
            and provider retention may affect final deletion.                                       
            Access can be revoked through the operator's Google Account                             
            permissions. Revoking access does not delete existing backups.                          
          </p>                                                                                      
          <h2>Contact</h2>                                                                          
          <p>                                                                                       
            Questions about this utility can be submitted through                                   
            <a href="https://github.com/thalsdj/Vault-Backup-Info/issues">                          
              the project's GitHub issue tracker</a>.                                               
            Do not submit private information, credentials, or backup                               
            contents in a public issue.                                                             
          </p>                                                                                      
          <p><a href="index.html">Home</a></p>                                                      
        </main>                                                                                     
      </body>                                                                                       
      </html>   
